        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="i-VnWK1uksur5Cd8t2WV-161" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;If an adversary controls all the nodes, then in theory, all &lt;br&gt;they need to do is watch what goes in and out, to be able to&lt;br&gt;determine the real location of every hidden service.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;they just need to keep making requests to the same hidden service&lt;br&gt;over a long stretch of time, logging all that goes in and out of the network,&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AND ESPECIALLY LOOKING AT THE SHAPE AND TIMING OF THE TRAFFIC ON BOTH ENDS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;to be able to have a very high likelihood of finding the location of the hidden service&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="650.5" y="1601" width="542" height="127" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
