        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iM8Zz2Tr5FXErz_H8n0_-66" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 128, 0);&quot;&gt;However, due to Node B,C,H,L,O,N,I, and E&lt;br&gt;being behind NATs, they can only talk to each other via&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#00ff00&quot;&gt;the public Nodes F,G,J and K.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 255);&quot;&gt;(UDP Hole-punching is also possible)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="406.5" y="3236.5" width="309" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iM8Zz2Tr5FXErz_H8n0_-67" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 128, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;AND&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ff8000&quot;&gt;this also helps with decoy destinations, since by that feature,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;every second-hop node can be a potential decoy destination,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ff8000&quot;&gt;either the second-hop nodes are actually recieving legit traffic,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;or they are recieving traffic that is meant to be forwarded back to public nodes,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ff8000&quot;&gt;or they are recieving traffic that is not meant for them (to be discarded)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="327" y="3298.5" width="469" height="98" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="J5L8lLLXnxCU2Hx9yfRl-1" value="&lt;u&gt;Detecting and rejecting any node&lt;br&gt;that misbehaves&lt;/u&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
