        <mxCell id="Ks_VO9Inp2RuTejZyS4B-114" value="For a path length of two 3-hop circuits&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;(D,G,J -&amp;gt; I), &lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 128, 0);&quot;&gt;the adversary needs to control:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;-the 6 real hops in between, (B,C,D,F,G,H)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;-AND the 2 final destination decoys of both circuits (P, O, W, X)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;(10 nodes for a path length of 2x3)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 128, 0);&quot;&gt;To be able to determine that Node A intended to talk to Node E&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;(Decoy Nodes I,J,K,L,M,N,Q,R,S,T,U,and V) are useless as decoys&lt;br&gt;if the adversary controlled B,C,D,F,G,H,P,O,W, and X) to begin with)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
