        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ks_VO9Inp2RuTejZyS4B-355" value="the current total path length for a given hidden service is 8&lt;br&gt;(6 nodes in between the client and the Hidden Service),&lt;br&gt;given the 2 circuits and their unidirectionnal nature,&lt;br&gt;it forms a circle which goes in one direction only" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-2613.93" y="2707" width="326" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ks_VO9Inp2RuTejZyS4B-356" value="Except that with probalistic path lengths &lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;(which can vary between 2 hops and 5 hops at random,&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;which means that the Client and Hidden service&lt;br&gt;can be at different places on the circle)" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-2551.93" y="2799" width="313" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ks_VO9Inp2RuTejZyS4B-357" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 128, 0);&quot;&gt;In this example, Node A randomly picked a 2&lt;br&gt;hop path to send packets to Node D,&lt;br&gt;meanwhile Node D randomly picked a 4 hop path &lt;br&gt;to send packets back to Node A&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-2536.43" y="2901" width="280" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
