        <mxCell id="Yh95EMxYVOAF0Q5FzLhY-273" value="8) which would result in the following positions:" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-7864" y="1488" width="267" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Yh95EMxYVOAF0Q5FzLhY-274" value="9) a hidden service&#39;s address on the hashring does not&lt;br&gt;reveal it&#39;s actual location, &lt;font&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ff0000&quot;&gt;it only reveals where it&#39;s rendezvous&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ff0000&quot;&gt;circuits would be.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font&gt;10) Therefore, Node A builds a 3 hop circuit to a Node&lt;br&gt;where Hidden Service A2 and A3 should be,&lt;br&gt;to establish a rendezvous point&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;11) the designated Node K acting as rendezvous point&lt;br&gt;is now tasked to relay back traffic to Node A&lt;br&gt;in case if they are asked to relay traffic for&lt;br&gt;the hidden service whose hash is &quot;44AWDAWDSWA&quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;strokeWidth=15;" parent="1" vertex="1">
