          <mxGeometry x="-7238" y="1990" width="242" height="41" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Yh95EMxYVOAF0Q5FzLhY-317" value="13) now you are Client V (Node V), and you want to&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;communicate to hidden service A2,&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;YOU KNOW the hidden service A2&#39;s address,&lt;br&gt;so you know that you&#39;re looking &lt;br&gt;for th&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;e&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: wrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;44AWDAWDSWA hash&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-7483.5" y="2284.5" width="295" height="84" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Yh95EMxYVOAF0Q5FzLhY-318" value="in order:&lt;br&gt;1) Node A establishes &lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;Node K&lt;/font&gt; as the RDV point for their&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;hidden service A3&lt;/font&gt; whose &lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;hash is 44AWDAWDSWA&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;2) client node V establishes &lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;Node Z&lt;/font&gt; as a rdv point for the &lt;font&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#9933ff&quot;&gt;Z12312AWDAW hash&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 236, 236);&quot;&gt;3) client V asks a random node (KN18) in the &quot;4*&quot; neighborhood &lt;br&gt;on the hashring for whoever knows where the RDV for the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;44AWDAWDSWA &lt;/span&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;hash is&lt;br&gt;4) client V&#39;s traffic gets routed to the RDV node in the 4* neighborhood, which then routes it back to Node A&lt;br&gt;5)Node A decrypts the traffic, and sees that the client&lt;br&gt;asks for the response to be routed back to&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#9933ff&quot;&gt; RDV node Z&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;6) The circuit is established:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;V&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;-&amp;gt;W1-&amp;gt;KN18-&amp;gt;KN4-&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;K&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;-&amp;gt;L-&amp;gt;M-&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;A&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;A&lt;/font&gt;-&amp;gt;A1-&amp;gt;A2-&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(153, 51, 255);&quot;&gt;Z&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;-&amp;gt;Y1-&amp;gt;Y2-&amp;gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;V&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;strokeWidth=15;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-6862" y="2400.25" width="366" height="366" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
